+ * (parser name, charset) - see ObGenDicLoader::get_dic_loader() - and the parser name here
+ * is always the constant "ik", because need_to_load_dic is only ever true for the ik
+ * parser (ObFtsIndexBuilderUtil::is_need_dictionary() is a case_compare against "ik"). So
+ * (ik, charset) is fully described by the charset and that is what is remembered below.
+ * Once ObTenantDicLoader::try_load_dictionary_in_trans() has succeeded for a charset it is
+ * a no-op for every later call (is_load_ is already set), and re-resolving the loader out
+ * of the map only takes a write lock, hashes the key and bumps a reference count. So the
+ * loaded charset is remembered here and the resolution is skipped. 0 means "not loaded
+ * yet"; any other charset - including an unsupported one - still runs the original code
+ * path, so the error behavior is unchanged. If a second dictionary backed parser is added
+ * later, this key must include its name.
+ */
+int64_t g_ik_dic_loaded_charset = 0;
